      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-00"
      },
      "source": [
        "# 07 ‚Äî SAM 3: Prompts de texto\n",
        "\n",
        "## ¬øQu√© vamos a construir hoy?\n",
        "\n",
        "Segmentar√°s objetos describiendo en texto lo que buscas ‚Äî sin necesitar un detector\n",
        "previo como YOLO. SAM 3 entiende el lenguaje natural y encuentra todas las instancias\n",
        "del concepto que le pidas en la imagen.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Aprender√°s a:**\n",
        "- Usar `SAM3SemanticPredictor` para prompts de texto\n",
        "- Comparar texto vs. bounding box: cu√°ndo conviene cada uno\n",
        "- Ajustar el umbral de confianza para controlar cu√°ntas detecciones obtienes\n",
        "- Ver el efecto de conceptos espec√≠ficos vs. gen√©ricos\n",
        "\n",
        "**Tiempo estimado:** 30 minutos"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "KhqAYXkduAzL"
      },
      "source": [
        "## ‚è±Ô∏è Estructura de la Clase (Duraci√≥n estimada: 1 hora)\n",
        "- **Introducci√≥n y Conceptos Base**: 15 min\n",
        "- **Desarrollo y Demostraci√≥n Pr√°ctica**: 25 min\n",
        "- **An√°lisis y Casos Extremos (Pausa y Observa)**: 20 min"
      ],
      "id": "KhqAYXkduAzL"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-01",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-01"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Texto como prompt\n",
        "\n",
        "En NB06 le d√°bamos a SAM las coordenadas de una caja: *\"el objeto est√° aqu√≠, segm√©ntalo\"*.\n",
        "Con SAM 3, tambi√©n puedes decirle: *\"encuentra y segmenta todo lo que sea una persona\"*.\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "Prompt bbox:  SAM(image, bboxes=[[100,50,300,400]])  ‚Üê t√∫ ya sabes d√≥nde est√°\n",
        "Prompt texto: predictor(text=[\"person\"])             ‚Üê SAM lo busca solo\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Cu√°ndo usar cada uno:\n",
        "- **Texto** ‚Üí no tienes detector previo, describes lo que buscas en lenguaje natural.\n",
        "- **Bbox** ‚Üí ya tienes un detector entrenado para tu dominio y quieres mayor precisi√≥n.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "4e921248",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4e921248"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "from google.colab import drive\n",
        "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
        "sam_path = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/RandD/Archive_Zero_Resolved/sam3.pt\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-02",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-02"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "!pip install supervision ultralytics\n",
        "import supervision as sv\n",
        "from ultralytics.models.sam import SAM3SemanticPredictor\n",
        "from ultralytics import YOLO, SAM\n",
        "import torch\n",
        "import cv2\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import urllib.request\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "Path(\"assets\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n",
        "urllib.request.urlretrieve(\"https://ultralytics.com/images/bus.jpg\",    \"assets/bus.jpg\")\n",
        "urllib.request.urlretrieve(\"https://ultralytics.com/images/zidane.jpg\", \"assets/zidane.jpg\")\n",
        "\n",
        "image = cv2.imread(\"assets/bus.jpg\")\n",
        "print(f\"Imagen cargada: {image.shape}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-03",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-03"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Paso 1: Cargar SAM3SemanticPredictor\n",
        "\n",
        "`SAM3SemanticPredictor` es el predictor especializado en prompts de texto y conceptos.\n",
        "Es distinto al `SAM()` gen√©rico que usamos en NB06 para bboxes.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "4db01119",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4db01119"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Los par√°metros de `overrides`\n",
        "\n",
        "El diccionario `overrides` configura c√≥mo funciona el predictor:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Par√°metro | Valor | Significado |\n",
        "|-----------|-------|-------------|\n",
        "| `conf` | `0.25` | Umbral de confianza m√≠nimo. Solo se incluyen detecciones con score ‚â• 0.25. Sube este valor para reducir falsos positivos; b√°jalo para capturar m√°s objetos. |\n",
        "| `task` | `\"segment\"` | Le dice a Ultralytics que el objetivo es segmentaci√≥n (no detecci√≥n simple ni clasificaci√≥n). |\n",
        "| `mode` | `\"predict\"` | Modo inferencia. Otras opciones son `\"train\"` y `\"val\"`, pero para usar el modelo siempre es `\"predict\"`. |\n",
        "| `model` | `\"sam3.pt\"` | Archivo de pesos del modelo. Si lo tienes en otra ruta, cambia este valor. |\n",
        "\n",
        "El par√°metro opcional `half=True` activa precisi√≥n FP16 (solo en GPU), lo que\n",
        "reduce el consumo de memoria y acelera la inferencia sin p√©rdida significativa de precisi√≥n."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-04",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-04"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "overrides = dict(conf=0.25, task=\"segment\", mode=\"predict\", model=sam_path)\n",
        "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "    overrides[\"half\"] = True   # FP16 solo en GPU\n",
        "\n",
        "predictor = SAM3SemanticPredictor(overrides=overrides)\n",
        "print(\"Predictor listo\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-05",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-05"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Paso 2: Inferencia con texto\n",
        "\n",
        "`predictor.set_image()` carga la imagen en memoria una sola vez.\n",
        "Despu√©s puedes hacer varias llamadas con distintos prompts sin recargarla.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-06",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-06"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "predictor.set_image(image)\n",
        "\n",
        "resultados = predictor(text=[\"person\"])[0]\n",
        "detections = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(resultados)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Objetos encontrados: {len(detections)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"¬øTiene m√°scaras?    {detections.mask is not None}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-07",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-07"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Paso 3: Visualizar\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-08",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-08"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "box_annotator  = sv.BoxAnnotator()\n",
        "mask_annotator = sv.MaskAnnotator(opacity=0.6)\n",
        "\n",
        "annotated = mask_annotator.annotate(scene=image.copy(), detections=detections)\n",
        "annotated = box_annotator.annotate(scene=annotated,    detections=detections)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
        "plt.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(annotated, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.title('SAM 3 con prompt de texto: \"person\"')\n",
        "plt.show()\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-09",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-09"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Pausa y observa: confianza por objeto\n",
        "\n",
        "A diferencia del pipeline YOLO ‚Üí SAM de NB06, aqu√≠ SAM 3 asigna\n",
        "directamente un score de confianza a cada m√°scara.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-10",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-10"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "if detections.confidence is not None:\n",
        "    for i, conf in enumerate(detections.confidence):\n",
        "        area = int(detections.mask[i].sum()) if detections.mask is not None else 0\n",
        "        print(f\"Objeto {i}: confianza={conf:.3f}  area={area:,} px2\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-11",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-11"
      },
      "source": [
        "## üîß Exploraci√≥n interactiva\n",
        "\n",
        "### Experimento 1: Concepto espec√≠fico vs. gen√©rico\n",
        "\n",
        "¬øSAM 3 devuelve m√°s o menos objetos cuando el concepto es m√°s amplio?\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-12",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-12"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n",
        "for ax, concepto in zip(axes, [\"vehicle\", \"bus\", \"person\"]):\n",
        "    res = predictor(text=[concepto])[0]\n",
        "    det = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(res)\n",
        "    scn = sv.MaskAnnotator(opacity=0.6).annotate(scene=image.copy(), detections=det)\n",
        "    ax.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(scn, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f'\"{concepto}\" ‚Äî {len(det)} objetos')\n",
        "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "# üí≠ Reflexi√≥n: ¬ø\"vehicle\" incluye el bus? ¬øQu√© ocurre con conceptos ambiguos?\n",
        "# Conceptos amplios capturan m√°s instancias pero pueden incluir falsos positivos.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-13",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-13"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Experimento 2: Umbral de confianza\n",
        "\n",
        "`conf` controla el umbral m√≠nimo para incluir una detecci√≥n.\n",
        "Podemos variarlo sin recargar el modelo.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-14",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-14"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n",
        "for ax, umbral in zip(axes, [0.1, 0.3, 0.6]):\n",
        "    predictor.args.conf = umbral\n",
        "    res = predictor(text=[\"person\"])[0]\n",
        "    det = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(res)\n",
        "    scn = sv.MaskAnnotator(opacity=0.6).annotate(scene=image.copy(), detections=det)\n",
        "    ax.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(scn, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f\"conf={umbral}  ({len(det)} objetos)\")\n",
        "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "predictor.args.conf = 0.25   # restaurar valor original\n",
        "# üí≠ Reflexi√≥n: ¬øQu√© umbral produce el mejor resultado visual?\n",
        "# Un umbral bajo puede incluir detecciones parciales en los bordes de la imagen.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-15",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-15"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Experimento 3: Texto vs. bounding box\n",
        "\n",
        "Compara las m√°scaras de SAM 3 cuando la gu√≠a es texto\n",
        "versus cuando son cajas de YOLO (como en NB06).\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-16",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-16"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "predictor.args.conf = 0.25\n",
        "res_texto   = predictor(text=[\"person\"])[0]\n",
        "det_texto   = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(res_texto)\n",
        "\n",
        "yolo_model  = YOLO(\"yolov8n.pt\")\n",
        "yolo_r      = yolo_model(image)[0]\n",
        "yolo_det    = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(yolo_r)\n",
        "solo_person = yolo_det[yolo_det.class_id == 0]\n",
        "sam_bbox    = SAM(sam_path)\n",
        "res_bbox    = sam_bbox(image, bboxes=solo_person.xyxy.tolist())[0]\n",
        "det_bbox    = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(res_bbox)\n",
        "\n",
        "scn_texto = sv.MaskAnnotator(opacity=0.6).annotate(scene=image.copy(), detections=det_texto)\n",
        "scn_bbox  = sv.MaskAnnotator(opacity=0.6).annotate(scene=image.copy(), detections=det_bbox)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(18, 7))\n",
        "ax1.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(scn_texto, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "ax1.set_title(f'Texto: \"person\" ({len(det_texto)} objetos)')\n",
        "ax1.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "ax2.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(scn_bbox, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "ax2.set_title(f\"Bbox YOLO ({len(det_bbox)} objetos)\")\n",
        "ax2.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"Texto vs. bounding box\", fontsize=13)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "# üí≠ Reflexi√≥n: ¬øCu√°l detecta m√°s personas? ¬øLas m√°scaras son igual de precisas?\n",
        "# El texto puede encontrar personas que YOLO no detect√≥ (mayor cobertura).\n",
        "# Las cajas de YOLO tienden a producir m√°scaras m√°s precisas en contornos.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cell-17",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-17"
      },
      "source": [
        "## üöÄ Reto de extensi√≥n\n",
        "\n",
        "**Tarea:** Para cada concepto (`\"person\"`, `\"bus\"`, `\"wheel\"`), encuentra\n",
        "el objeto con mayor √°rea de m√°scara y mu√©stralo en una figura de 1√ó3.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Pista:**\n",
        "```python\n",
        "if detections.mask is not None:\n",
        "    areas   = detections.mask.sum(axis=(1, 2))  # pixeles True por mascara\n",
        "    idx_max = int(areas.argmax())\n",
        "    mayor   = detections[idx_max]\n",
        "```\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cell-18",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cell-18"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Escribe tu soluci√≥n aqu√≠\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 5))\n",
        "for ax, concepto in zip(axes, [\"person\", \"bus\", \"wheel\"]):\n",
        "    res = predictor(text=[concepto])[0]\n",
        "    det = sv.Detections.from_ultralytics(res)\n",
        "    if det.mask is not None and len(det) > 0:\n",
        "        areas   = det.mask.sum(axis=(1, 2))   # √°rea en p√≠xeles de cada m√°scara\n",
        "        idx_max = int(areas.argmax())          # √≠ndice del objeto m√°s grande\n",
        "        mayor   = det[idx_max]                 # sv.Detections con 1 objeto\n",
        "        # annotated = mask_annotator.annotate(scene=image.copy(), detections=mayor)\n",
        "        # ax.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(annotated, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "    ax.imshow(cv2.cvtColor(image.copy(), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB))\n",
        "    ax.set_title(f'\"{concepto}\"')\n",
        "    ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ]
    },
